        # bun.lock is not a wholesale replacement (bash/zsh): the change is
        # far smaller than either version's total line count
        git show base-snapshot/v2.46.0:bun.lock | wc -l
        git show HEAD:bun.lock | wc -l
        git diff --no-index --numstat \
          <(git show base-snapshot/v2.46.0:bun.lock) <(git show HEAD:bun.lock)

    **With license texts of that kind set aside, the conclusion is not
    weakened**: **those files as a whole may only be distributed under the
    terms of AGPL-3.0-or-later** -- the text entries as combined works,
    because the Qianmo portion inside them is an AGPL work; the six `.node`
