    There are three reasons for not adding headers to them. First, the header
    marks **which layer a file came from**, not who wrote which line: a file
    that came from the base project and was afterwards modified by Qianmo is
    still a file of base provenance. Second, **this is a marking convention we
    set ourselves, not something MIT demands of us**: what MIT asks is that the
    license and copyright notice be *included in copies*, which this repository
    discharges through the verbatim `LICENSE.base`; it does not forbid us from
    putting other identifiers on a file, and an SPDX line erases nothing. We
    leave them off so that "header / no header" keeps meaning **the provenance
